    {
      "description": "Set up an isolated worktree lane over the repositories the run covers, from what each declares in the configuration's resource table: worktrees, ports, databases, cache-store index, dependencies, and seed data. Idempotent — re-running keeps the lane's allocation and never reseeds existing databases.",
      "name": "provision",
    },
    {
      "description": "Remove a provisioned lane across every declared repository: its processes (by exact pid, only those listening on the lane's ports from inside its worktrees that this session or an ended one started), its cache-store index, its whole database family including derived names, and its worktrees. Refuses a lane another live Claude Code session is using, or one with uncommitted changes; never touches the branch.",
      "name": "teardown",
